1
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten up,
and try stepping back for a look.

2
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:28,640
Like someone is calling out to you,
an afternoon after the rain.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
hand in hand with Mom.

4
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:42,500
That mysterious feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,720
So on the arcade's guide tiles,

6
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,100
Even the self-important politicians
and the blue-eyeshadowed aunties.

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there is Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:40,500
Transformed Commoner Nakagawa-kun

16
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:45,560
Kei-chan is changing his lifestyle?

17
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:50,580
Yes, from now on I'm also aiming to live
as much like an ordinary person as I can.

18
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:52,880
Why did you suddenly decide that?

19
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:57,020
Actually, I attended a company
board meeting the other day,

20
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,660
and our Nakagawa Group,
ahead of other companies,

21
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:04,260
quickly launched company-wide,
bone-deep cost cutting

22
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:07,800
and large-scale, innovative recession measures.
As a result,

23
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:11,696
railways, hotels, banks, real estate,

24
00:02:11,746 --> 00:02:14,840
automobiles, and securities,
the performance of every division

25
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,660
has steadily recovered.

26
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:20,900
This is entirely thanks to
your efforts in management.

27
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:25,020
As a token of my gratitude,
I've prepared a gift for all of you today.

28
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,260
I bought this with my own pocket money.

29
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,140
Please enjoy it without holding back.

30
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:41,240
It's time for my energy drink refill.

31
00:02:58,340 --> 00:03:01,340
Hm? Hm?

32
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:05,260
Here it comes, here it comes, here it comes!

33
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:06,160
It's here!

34
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:15,220
While serving us super-luxury champagne,

35
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:19,500
the president himself swapped his
custom energy drink for cheap eggs

36
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,400
and kept up with that grueling workload.

37
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,420
I'd love to join you for a toast,

38
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:28,460
but I have a meeting for
the 21st Century Project

39
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:30,840
and I must head to my next destination.

40
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,400
That's all.

41
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,900
A toast to President Ryuichiro Nakagawa!

42
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:35,720
Cheers!

43
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,420
Seeing my father's flexible attitude,

44
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:44,620
I felt I learned what a person
in charge should be like.

45
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,800
So I thought about what I could do,

46
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,240
and first,
to set an example for the other employees,

47
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,660
I decided to review the waste around me.

48
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:53,980
You're amazing, Kei-chan.

49
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,820
It's only just beginning.

50
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:58,760
You're admirable as a businessman.

51
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,380
Senpai, what's wrong?

52
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,020
What is it?

53
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:05,660
Isn't it obvious?

54
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:08,380
Senpai, what are you doing in the kitchen?

55
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:09,780
Isn't it obvious just by looking?

56
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:11,160
Ryo-chan, you're the worst.

57
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,620
What's wrong with rinsing
off and washing myself here?

58
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:16,080
Ryo-san,
you'd better put your clothes on quickly.

59
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,940
If the Chief comes,
there'll be trouble again.

60
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,060
Alright, alright, I'm coming out right now.

61
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,220
Living like the common
folk is harder than it looks

62
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,540
What on earth were you thinking?

63
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,820
Yes, as a start,
I swapped my beloved Ferrari for a Porsche.

64
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:31,460
I also switched my gasoline
from high-octane to regular.

65
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,980
Even as a joke,
it's not funny in the slightest.

66
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,620
I'm not joking at all.

67
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,740
I'm seriously aiming for
a down-to-earth lifestyle,

68
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:39,640
Are you getting used to it?

69
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,940
The Porsche part is what's down-to-earth,
you know.

70
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,660
Give up the cars and commute by train.

71
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:44,900
Trains are

72
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,880
When I was a kid, I rode a train once
as part of a hands-on learning program,

73
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:52,600
but that was only once,
accompanying my tutor.

74
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,180
Hands-on learning?

75
00:04:54,540 --> 00:05:00,220
So you probably don't even know that most of
Tokyo's stations have automatic ticket gates now?

76
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:03,720
What? Really?
Even Tokyo, which was said to be impossible?

77
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,020
You're hopelessly out of touch.

78
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:09,700
If you're the heir to the Nakagawa Group,
I suppose it can't be helped.

79
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:13,520
Well, since I drive a Porsche too,
I'm on Nakagawa's side.

80
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:18,560
You two are secretly looking down on the
commoners who ride trains and laughing at them.

81
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:21,101
No, Ryo! Even if he's never ridden a train,

82
00:05:21,151 --> 00:05:24,420
I'm saying Kei-chan is a kind man who
understands other people's feelings!

83
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:27,160
That's right, he's far more humble
and admirable than you, Ryo-san!

84
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:31,360
What?! Please don't fight over me,
all three of you.

85
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:33,686
Well, let me say just this much.

86
00:05:33,736 --> 00:05:36,740
What happens when a spoiled brat
like you takes over as president?

87
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:39,452
A small flaw will spread
throughout the entire group,

88
00:05:39,502 --> 00:05:42,280
and eventually it will become irreversible!

89
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,700
Ryo-chan, that's mean.

90
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,580
I'm only giving you this
advice for Nakagawa's sake.

91
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,820
It just looks like you're
enjoying teasing him.

92
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:52,860
If it's Senpai, we have to cheer him on.

93
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:53,940
Cheer him on?

94
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:56,980
Cheering on the Nakagawa Group's heir.

95
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,980
The faint smell of money.

96
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,560
Relax, Nakagawa.

97
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:03,360
The reason I said such harsh things

98
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,400
is that I'm going to thoroughly

99
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:09,360
drill the basics of
common-folk life into you.

100
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,000
You, Senpai?

101
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,000
The authority on frugality.

102
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,580
Common-folk life advisor, Kankichi Ryotsu.

103
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,460
Now that I'm on your side,

104
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,420
rest easy,
as if you've already climbed aboard.

105
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,200
Don't get on board!

106
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:26,880
Let's start by fixing this flashy outfit.

107
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,540
What are you doing?

108
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:31,160
Just listen to what I say.

109
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,320
Senpai

110
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:40,900
This really is too short in the length,
isn't it.

111
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,460
A character as far removed
from the common folk as you

112
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:46,600
needs to be a little bit lacking
to strike the right balance.

113
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:47,460
That's ridiculous.

114
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,700
By the way, Nakagawa, you pay for
all your meals with a card, right?

115
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:55,620
Yes, basically I pay 100% by card.

116
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:59,680
Out of curiosity, do you know how
much the dinner you ate yesterday cost?

117
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:05,140
Last night it was Italian, and I think it was 40,000...
no, 50,000 yen.

118
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:09,100
Sorry, I don't check
small amounts like that.

119
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:12,140
That's exactly what it means to be
far removed from common-folk sense.

120
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,880
Nakagawa, hand over all the cards you have.

121
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:17,680
All of them?

122
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,180
All of them.

123
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:20,740
Understood.

124
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,560
You've got quite a few.

125
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,940
They're all gold and platinum cards.

126
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,300
From today, cut ties with your cards.

127
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,440
What are you going to do?

128
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,520
Pay in cash every time.

129
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,020
That's how you cut your spending.

130
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:33,940
It's the first step
toward common-folk living.

131
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:36,740
Understood.

132
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:39,160
When you know exactly how much money
Translation>
you have on you, like I do,

133
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,320
down to the last yen,

134
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,960
ramen and gyoza,

135
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:45,020
you can focus with all your might
Translation>
on choosing between menu items of the same price.

136
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:47,560
(see above)

137
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,700
What's the big deal? Especially

138
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:53,020
when you rarely get to order
gyoza and ramen together,

139
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:58,320
you feel like you've conquered the world.
Is that all it takes?

140
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:00,740
When you have no money
but are terribly hungry,

141
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:03,520
it's fried rice, fried rice, rice.

142
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:07,180
You mix a large portion of
rice into the fried rice,

143
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:11,580
and eat double.
But there's no need to mix it yourself,

144
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:13,740
you could just order two fried rices, right?

145
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:17,860
Are you Marie Antoinette?
The prices are different, the prices!

146
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,918
Ordering two fried rices
costs over 1,000 yen,

147
00:08:20,968 --> 00:08:24,580
but one fried rice and a
large rice saves you 350 yen.

148
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,380
I see.

149
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:31,300
Since I paid by card, I never needed to
calculate the exact amounts, so I just... didn't.

150
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:35,880
You're used to running your family business,
so these amounts may seem trivial to you, but...

151
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:41,660
Keeping track of every 10 and 20 yen is
what smart common-folk living is all about.

152
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,400
Yes, I understand.

153
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:45,480
What? You don't have any money?

154
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:50,220
I've paid for everything with cards until now,
so I have no cash at all.

155
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:54,460
I just remembered, senpai, you lent
me 3,000 yen the other day, didn't you?

156
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:56,840
If you pay that back to me, I can cover it.

157
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,380
What?

158
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:01,920
Damn, I should have made him pay here
first before getting rid of his cards.

159
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:05,780
Here, it's 2,550 yen after
subtracting the ramen money.

160
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,060
Sorry.

161
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,800
Senpai?

162
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:09,980
What, you've got it, right?

163
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:12,960
This 1,000 yen bill isn't Itō Hirobumi,
you know.

164
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:15,700
Is this really a 1,000 yen bill?

165
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,540
Are you messing with me?

166
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:19,000
The design changed over ten years ago,
you know.

167
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:21,460
Is that so?

168
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:24,020
No, it's just been a
while since I last saw one.

169
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:26,120
How do you even work as
a police officer with that?

170
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,280
Wait, could this be...

171
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:29,920
What is it this time?

172
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:32,860
Don't tell me you don't even
know what a 500 yen coin is.

173
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,640
So this is a 500 yen coin after all?

174
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,500
Wait, what era are you from?

175
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:41,220
Try living on that money this month.

176
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:45,040
It's 2,550 yen.

177
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:47,300
But there's still half a month left.

178
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:48,940
It's only half a month, isn't it?

179
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:50,260
Don't worry.

180
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:52,660
I've secured a place for you to sleep.

181
00:09:52,660 --> 00:09:53,980
Really?

182
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,300
Here.

183
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,420
Isn't this Nikoniko Dorm?

184
00:09:58,420 --> 00:09:59,600
That's right, and

185
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:02,580
you'll be sleeping in
this room starting today.

186
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:05,100
Isn't this your room, senpai?

187
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:05,600
That's right.

188
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,360
If it's 100 yen a night,

189
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:10,260
it's far cheaper than the
transportation costs to your own home.

190
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:12,360
You're charging money?

191
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,020
This room,
which only looks dirty at first glance,

192
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:20,980
is packed with household wisdom based on
the philosophy of frugality and products.

193
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:21,720
For example,

194
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:27,060
This is it!

195
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,040
Isn't that just bean sprouts?

196
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:32,840
Right, first plant the bean sprouts
you bought in a sponge soaked in water.

197
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,780
Grow them to double their
size before eating them.

198
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:40,680
Plant green onions and parsley in soil like this,
and they'll last a whole season.

199
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:46,000
Always grab pocket tissues
and various free samples.

200
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:49,520
The New Year's lucky draws
at the shopping street.

201
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:52,500
And service info like grand opening sales.

202
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:55,280
Keep a constant eye out
for prize contest ads too.

203
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,660
Don't forget to diligently
send in your postcards.

204
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,420
Back when I was still
stuck in that situation,

205
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:02,920
I was saved by prize products
more times than I can count.

206
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:04,860
But in your case,

207
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:09,160
it's a luxurious make-believe poverty life,
a part of your social education.

208
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,680
I'm serious.

209
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:14,300
For a while, I'll also cut off
contact with my family and the company.

210
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:17,700
Alright, I understand. It's a tough road,
so make sure you do your duty properly.

211
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:25,120
I've only got 350 yen, and there are still four or five days until the end of the month.
What am I going to do?

212
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,820
Here you go, Kei-chan. Your tea.

213
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:27,980
Thank you. Sorry.

214
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,360
Kei-chan,
another convenience store rice ball?

215
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:33,080
Yes, they're quick, cheap, and easy.

216
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,400
Since I started eating
convenience store meals,

217
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:38,020
I've been discovering all sorts of things.

218
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:44,500
Even with rice balls, the prices, flavors, and even how
the seaweed is wrapped vary subtly from store to store.

219
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:49,420
For example, pulling the wrapper apart from both sides,
or pulling out the thin paper inside.

220
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,440
But today I discovered
something even better.

221
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:54,920
Ta-da!

222
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:59,320
The classic three-pack with the seaweed
already wrapped is incredibly cheap.

223
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:05,120
For me, someone who likes the seaweed soggy, this is the perfect item.
It's a dream come true.

224
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,620
Kei-chan,
you're more adaptable than I thought.

225
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:13,420
I have something to deliver to the Chief,
so I'm leaving the rest to you.

226
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,940
Yes, understood.

227
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:17,520
Excuse me.

228
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:18,920
Yes, what's wrong?

229
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:22,040
It seems I dropped my wallet somewhere.

230
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,500
Right, that's the lost item report done.

231
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:29,400
Then, once that's done,
could I borrow some train fare?

232
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,700
That's a problem, isn't it.

233
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:32,960
How much would I need to buy a ticket?

234
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,160
About 350 yen should do it.

235
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:38,520
Good, 350 yen is exactly what I have.

236
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,540
Understood.

237
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,420
Then take this and get home safely.

238
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:43,320
Thank you very much.

239
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:45,740
You idiot.

240
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:49,080
What were you thinking, lending your
emergency money to a complete stranger?

241
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,920
Well, we are police officers at a neighborhood station,
so it's only natural.

242
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:53,440
I'll cover it.

243
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,100
No way.

244
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:56,820
That rich kid has no idea how hard
common-folk life in the city is.

245
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,500
Even if your wallet is completely empty,

246
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:02,600
you just assume someone will bail you out.

247
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:06,560
No, I only wanted to help
someone who was in trouble -

248
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:08,680
The one in trouble right now is you!

249
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:14,720
You say you gave 350 yen,
your lifeline, to a passerby.

250
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:17,080
Do you have any idea how reckless that was?

251
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:19,380
Helping people is a million
years too early for you.

252
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,600
I'm going to go cool my head for a bit.

253
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:32,540
You say you gave 350 yen,
a huge sum, to a total stranger.

254
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,080
Do you have any idea
how unfortunate that is!

255
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,823
The owner probably won't turn up, but

256
00:14:05,873 --> 00:14:07,320
we'll hold onto it for now.

257
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:10,680
No one would have known if you'd kept quiet.
What a hopelessly good-natured fool you are.

258
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:14,780
I thought long and hard about
what my senior said last night.

259
00:14:15,380 --> 00:14:18,880
But I still think what I did was right.

260
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:22,800
You stubborn fool.
Either way, payday is in four or five days.

261
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:24,820
Skipping a meal won't kill you.

262
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:27,740
Delicious.

263
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,700
Patience, patience.

264
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:36,260
Turn at that corner and head to the right

265
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:39,060
It's too pitiful to watch.

266
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,960
You're being unfair!

267
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:43,620
When I'm hungry,
you just pretend not to notice.

268
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:46,880
Just because you treated Nakagawa to a meal,
you're being overprotective.

269
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:50,620
Well, unlike Ryo-chan,
Kei-chan is delicately made, you know.

270
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:51,660
It's the same thing, the same thing!

271
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:53,320
Same human, same man.

272
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,660
Ryo-san's case is self-inflicted, isn't it?

273
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:57,000
Nakagawa-kun...

274
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:57,740
Shut up!

275
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:00,380
Damn it, that's special treatment, Nakagawa!

276
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,420
I'll find you a part-time job.

277
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:04,100
Yes, please.

278
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:07,000
Go ahead and really whip him into shape.

279
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:08,760
What's your name?

280
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:11,260
Yes, my name is Keiichi Nakagawa.

281
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:12,120
Nakagawa.

282
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:16,240
With all this rain lately,
we're behind schedule, so it'll be tough.

283
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:17,800
Yes, I'll do my best.

284
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,440
Then I'll take him under my wing, Ryo-san.

285
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,860
Alright, I'm counting on you.

286
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:23,440
Nakagawa, wait here a moment.

287
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,060
Yes.

288
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,720
How do you know his name?

289
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:32,080
So it all turns out to be your company's

290
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,420
It was a site belonging to my company.

291
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:37,480
If you're really the heir
to the Nakagawa Group,

292
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,780
everyone's going to be blown away.

293
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:40,060
I know.

294
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:41,600
I won't say a word,
not even if you tore my mouth open.

295
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:42,960
Hey, Kawanaka.

296
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,460
Yes?

297
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,560
This is Kawanaka,
who'll be helping us out for the day.

298
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:52,340
Take-san, please look after him for us.

299
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:53,800
It's rough, you know.

300
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,080
You alright, kid?

301
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,420
Yes, nice to meet you.

302
00:15:58,280 --> 00:15:59,000
Nice to meet you.

303
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,860
The fried rice from that time...

304
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:08,900
What?

305
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:11,860
Are you Mr. Nakagawa's boss?

306
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:13,580
What is it?

307
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:15,400
Here, this is my card.

308
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:17,340
Kankodori Industries.

309
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:18,840
Hachinosu Real Estate.

310
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,240
Dandanba Contractors.

311
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:22,900
Everyone came to see Kei-chan, you know.

312
00:16:23,460 --> 00:16:25,580
to the next president of the Nakagawa Group,

313
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:27,540
I think they want to get in touch with him.

314
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:28,300
I see.

315
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:30,800
Unfortunately,
Mr. Nakagawa is out at the moment.

316
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,820
As his superior and family,
I'll take your message.

317
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:36,860
Are you a relative?

318
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:39,920
Yes, indeed.
My younger brother Kinjirō's wife is

319
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:43,940
Nakagawa's grandmother's younger sister's
son's ex-wife's daughter's eldest son's

320
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:46,860
second wife's younger brother's daughter.

321
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:49,140
Ryo-san, how about alcohol?

322
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,500
I drink in moderation.

323
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,600
How often do you play golf?

324
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:54,200
I go round and round.

325
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:55,900
What's your favorite food?

326
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:56,720
Beef bowl.

327
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,420
No, steak.

328
00:16:58,420 --> 00:16:59,860
And Matsusaka beef, too.

329
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:01,580
I wonder what he plans to do?

330
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:02,500
Well...

331
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:10,520
Hey! Where are you looking, buddy!

332
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:11,220
Over here!

333
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:12,940
S-sorry.

334
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:16,880
How's the job? Not easy, is it?

335
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,360
Yeah.

336
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,120
You're a cop, aren't you?

337
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:21,200
Did you get hooked on
a card loan or something?

338
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:26,420
No, I overheard you talking
about that at the ramen shop, so...

339
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:30,180
Well there's a lot of backstory to this...

340
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,980
Nah, you look serious,
so I'll teach you a few things.

341
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:34,560
Thanks.

342
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:43,860
Hey, Yama,
handle the traffic direction out front.

343
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:44,820
Yes, sir.

344
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:47,120
We're doing traffic control too?

345
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:50,660
Yeah, with this recession,
they're cutting security staff costs too.

346
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:52,240
Even that far?

347
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:54,380
Tanaka, help Yama out too.

348
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:54,840
Yes.

349
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:00,920
This is Nakagawa, who looks up
to me like a real older brother.

350
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:03,220
He'll do whatever I say.

351
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,380
Yes, go ahead.

352
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:06,440
Come on, come on, come on.

353
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:07,440
Big brother, something's off.

354
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:11,280
Sorry, we'll get you through right away.

355
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,680
Hey, hurry up and come through.

356
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,560
Come on, come on.

357
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,880
Excuse me,
can you get out to the national highway?

358
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:17,820
That's right.

359
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:19,240
I'll guide you through now.

360
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:21,980
Come on, come on, come on.

361
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,980
Haaah!

362
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:27,180
Come on, come on!

363
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,860
Back and forth again today!

364
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:32,180
Yamamoto-san!
Then we'll let this one through first!

365
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:34,220
Got it! Just wait a sec!

366
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:35,080
OK!

367
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,180
Go ahead! Sorry for the long wait!

368
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,260
Go ahead!

369
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,740
That part-timer's not half bad, is he!

370
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:43,220
Yeah!

371
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:48,160
Nakagawa, when I, your advisor, say
"right," what do you say?

372
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:48,700
Right!

373
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:49,960
And when I say "left"?

374
00:18:50,140 --> 00:18:50,440
Left!

375
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:54,220
That means the group is
in the palm of my hand.

376
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,620
Alright, lunchtime!

377
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,380
A part-time job with a
lunch box is a real help.

378
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:00,520
Lucky you.

379
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:03,740
If only this made the construction
schedule a little easier.

380
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:06,660
Yeah, with this schedule
there's no way we'll make it.

381
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:08,000
Is it really that tight?

382
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,600
With the crew we have now, yeah.

383
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,480
Understood, I'll go let the higher-ups know.

384
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:15,440
What's this, kid,
you know the site supervisor?

385
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:18,260
N-no, well, hey kid, want a drink?

386
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:20,540
Yes... where's the cup?

387
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:24,440
You just cover the hole in the
lid with your finger like this,

388
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:29,600
and it's delicious!

389
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:32,900
One more cup!

390
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:40,300
As expected,
Maru's richness is on another level.

391
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,060
Foie gras, caviar, steak.

392
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:46,040
Treating us to such a feast in broad daylight,
I feel bad.

393
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:51,640
Son, what do you want to be in the future?

394
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:53,260
My future?

395
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:56,340
This guy's going to be a great architect,
right, Yama?

396
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:57,480
Stop it.

397
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:00,320
I'm attending the night program
at the technical university now.

398
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:05,180
I'm planning to apply to Nakagawa
Construction's design office next year,

399
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,060
but that place is super competitive.

400
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:10,140
Yama has a different
eye than the other guys.

401
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:14,620
The other day you said you wanted
to build a zoo-hotel combo, right?

402
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,480
It was just a passing idea.

403
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,760
That's interesting.

404
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:20,240
If I were the president,
I'd hire you on the spot.

405
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:22,620
I'd like to hire you.

406
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:24,040
No, no.

407
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,680
You look just like a company president, kid.

408
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:26,220
It was...

409
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,280
Are you gonna say it? Are you gonna say it?

410
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:31,440
Well, shall we get going?

411
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,520
Maybe Ginza this time?

412
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:34,040
Or maybe Akasaka?

413
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,800
Before that,
we're going to Nakagawa Junior's place.

414
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,320
Right, that's right.

415
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,100
Alright, leave it to me.

416
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,840
Alright, that's it for today.

417
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:44,760
Finally, we're done, we're done.

418
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:46,040
Today was tough

419
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,020
Are you okay?

420
00:20:47,020 --> 00:20:48,560
Y-yes, I'm fine.

421
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:51,880
Here he is, over here!

422
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:56,140
Mr. Mikura of the Nakagawa Group is here,
of all places!

423
00:20:56,140 --> 00:20:57,980
Hey, Nakagawa!

424
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:00,420
Senpai, that man is -

425
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:01,640
Nakagawa Junior!

426
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:05,280
As a family member, I've brought
you a business proposal, Nakagawa!

427
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:06,540
Nakagawa!

428
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:08,420
You've got the name wrong.

429
00:21:08,420 --> 00:21:09,180
Nakagawa!

430
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:13,200
Please, do pass along a word to your father.

431
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:15,880
No, that's troublesome, I'm just -

432
00:21:16,540 --> 00:21:17,500
I see.

433
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:20,600
The son of the Nakagawa Group's chairman,
no less!

434
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:22,240
Even if you held a gun to my head,
I wouldn't say a word.

435
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:26,200
Senpai is testing whether
I'll keep that secret.

436
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,240
Who's this Nakagawa, anyway?

437
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,420
I'm Kawanaka, Kawanaka!

438
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:33,060
Kawanaka and Kawanaka, that's right.

439
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,620
Don't move around for no reason!

440
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:35,640
Except for one hour, you know.

441
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,640
So what exactly is going on?

442
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,840
Were you deceiving us?

443
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:43,480
Nakagawa, please, tell us the truth.

444
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:46,340
Senpai, you're testing my guts, aren't you?

445
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:48,040
I won't fall for that.

446
00:21:48,820 --> 00:21:51,130
Senpai, you're joking again.

447
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:53,540
I'm Kawanaka. Kawanaka!

448
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:57,120
It's true, I swear.
I'm not lying. Believe me.

449
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:58,820
Anyway, let's talk over there.

450
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:02,300
He's the real heir to the Nakagawa Group,
I tell you.

451
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:07,017
For you,
who deal with people's business every day,

452
00:22:07,067 --> 00:22:09,580
it may be a trifling sum.

453
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:13,520
Maybe he really is from
the Nakagawa Group...

454
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:17,340
Hey, Kawanaka.
Here's today's pay. Come and get it.

455
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:20,500
Thanks for everything today.

456
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:21,840
You really saved me.

457
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:22,880
See you again sometime.

458
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:23,660
Someday.

459
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:24,880
Nakagawa.

460
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,000
You're still going on about it?

461
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:26,720
Help me.

462
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:27,300
Look.

463
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:28,840
Ryo-chan.

464
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,460
I'm ordering lunch delivery, though.

465
00:22:30,460 --> 00:22:32,600
Matsusaka beef steak.

466
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:36,020
There's no such thing in Tsurukame Prefecture,
Ryo-san.

467
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:38,260
Like I could eat ramen now.

468
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,640
Save your luxuries until
you've paid for them.

469
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:43,520
Damn, they entertained us without asking,
didn't they?

470
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:45,600
And then they had the
nerve to send us an invoice!

471
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:48,200
Kei-chan, what'll you have?

472
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:51,960
I'll make myself something with that and eat it,
so I don't need any.

473
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:55,440
Kei-chan, you've really gotten tough,
haven't you?

474
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:56,540
Is that so?

475
00:22:56,540 --> 00:23:00,480
Geez, that brat! Rich people should just
eat pricey stuff like rich people do.

476
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:03,640
That steak was good, wasn't it?

477
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:06,920
Delivery for Inspector Nakagawa.

478
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:08,620
Nakagawa?

479
00:23:08,620 --> 00:23:10,180
Yes, please sign here.

480
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:13,040
Yes! I won the prize draw!

481
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:16,820
I followed my senior's
advice and sent in a postcard.

482
00:23:30,340 --> 00:23:39,260
Dad, what's going on? Come on, look! This
cat's holding a real gold coin in its mouth!

483
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:45,260
What? To Mr. Nakagawa, the honest man who turned in a 100-yen coin he found,
a reward of 1 million yen!

484
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:46,140
What?

485
00:23:47,040 --> 00:23:48,260
One million yen!

486
00:23:48,940 --> 00:23:49,414
In the end,

487
00:23:49,464 --> 00:23:53,660
Nakagawa-kun is destined to become
rich no matter how things turn out.

488
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:55,380
Compared to that,

489
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:59,360
Shāto, mairudo, doberī

490
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:03,742
Alarm clock, kicking the clock,

491
00:24:03,792 --> 00:24:05,520
my little toe, ow ow

492
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:11,476
First I draw my eyebrows,
then I dance all the way to the station,

493
00:24:11,526 --> 00:24:13,740
dance, dance.

494
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:19,520
Dozing off on the train,
backs turned toward the road home,

495
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:25,820
another tough week,
and overwork is only natural.

496
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:33,180
Playing it cool with a bucket in hand, but
the beef bowl's broth is cloudy and extra soggy.

497
00:24:33,780 --> 00:24:40,200
Endless overtime frustration,
cleared up with more frustration.

498
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:08,760
Thank you for watching.

499
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:13,000
Monday

500
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:23,680
This is the one Nakagawa's
company developed,

501
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:25,980
a life simulation game
where you raise yourself

502
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:28,200
Alright, let's all give it a try!

503
